# Line endings.
#
# Git normalises text files to LF in the repository and checks them out with
# the platform's endings. That is right for source, and wrong for one file
# here: whatsapp.cmd uses labels (`call :use`, `goto :eof`), and cmd.exe seeks
# labels by byte offset. In an LF-only batch file that seek can land in the
# wrong place, so the script fails in ways that look random. The .cmd is
# therefore pinned to CRLF wherever it is checked out.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Everything else: let Git decide, and keep these explicitly LF so a Windows
# checkout does not rewrite files the build reads byte for byte.
* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Binary. Never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.yxi binary
*.yxmd binary
*.sqlite3 binary
